ate,random], seeds=10, leakage_guard=true): surrogate median 34.0 calcs, 2.99×; guard-off 3.12× (record d35524bb). (B) surrogate_error_by_family(leakage_guard=true): other 7.33%, chalcogenide 5.37%, pnictide 5.06%, halide 4.48%, oxide 3.32% (prior record 940537f1, confirmed unchanged). (C) test_prefilter series — gap[0.7,1.2]+elements: 21/129=16.3% (record 60c963a4); gap[0.7,1.8]+elements: 24/129=18.6%; gap[0.5,1.8]+elements: 36/129=27.9%; gap[0.7,1.2] only: 46/129=35.7%; elements only: 50/129=38.8%; gap[0.3,2.0]+elements: 43/129=33.3%; gap[0.5,1.5] only: 79/129=61.2%; gap[0.3,2.0] only: 105/129=81.4%. Dataset: 1362 candidates, 129 hits, 9.47% base rate (record f0f51395). Literature: OptB88vdW underestimation documented; ns² cation SLME families (doi:10.1039/c6cc06475b, doi:10.1038/s41467-022-32669-3).", "agent_generated_hypothesis": false}, {"id": "446d6d88", "time": "2026-10-03T18:34:23", "kind": "critique", "agent": "skeptic", "summary": "VERDICT: H1 pre-filter NOT TRUSTED. Abort gate TRUSTED. Round 1 BO surrogate (2.99×) TRUSTED WITH CAVEATS. The element filter (ns² cations) is the dominant recall killer: gap[0.7,1.2]+elements yields 16.3% recall (21/129) in a 41-candidate sub-pool. Gap-only [0.5,1.5] eV yields 61.2% recall (79/129) in 275 candidates at 28.7% base rate — barely above the 60% abort gate. Adding direct_gap=True would further reduce, not rescue, the recall. Round 1 leakage confirmed minor (Δ0.5 calc). OptB88vdW gap [0.7,1.2] eV is systematically too narrow for JARVIS SLME hits; the literature mapping does not hold for this pool.", "evidence": "Prefilter decomposition: gap[0.7,1.2]+elements: 41 cands, 16.3% recall; gap[0.7,1.2] only: 124 cands, 35.7% recall; elements only: 277 cands, 38.8% recall; gap[0.5,1.5] only: 275 cands, 61.2% recall, 28.7% base rate; gap[0.3,2.0] only: 448 cands, 81.4% recall. Leakage guard off/on: 33.3±2.5 vs 33.8±1.8 calcs (Δ<0.3σ). surrogate_error_by_family: Other 7.33%, Chalcogenide 5.37%, Pnictide 5.06%, Halide 4.48%, Oxide 3.32%. Runner record: 60c963a4. Previous skeptic: 7ba476fb.", "agent_generated_hypothesis": false}, {"id": "eef0c983", "time": "2026-10-03T18:34:28", "kind": "next_step", "agent": "director", "summary": "Round 3 experiment: test recalibrated gap-only pre-filter [0.5, 1.5] eV (no element constraint) + BO surrogate. Call compare_strategies(strategies=[random,surrogate], seeds=10, leakage_guard=True, gap_min=0.5, gap_max=1.5) on the 275-candidate filtered sub-pool (61.2% recall, 28.7% base rate). If surrogate speedup ≥3.5× vs full-pool random (106.8 calcs), H3 pipeline is salvageable with the recalibrated filter and we authorize live Option C (≤20 oracle calcs). If not, pivot to H2 heteroscedastic GP on the full 1,362-candidate pool.", "evidence": "Skeptic critique record 70a8f8dd. Gap-only [0.5,1.5] eV: 275 candidates, 61.2% recall, 28.7% base rate (3.0× enrichment). Full-pool random baseline: 106.8 calcs (record 05099ec9). H2 alternative: heteroscedastic GP to reduce chalcogenide MAE from 5.37% to ≤3.8% (record ad24f734).", "agent_generated_hypothesis": false}, {"id": "24c79e53", "time": "2026-10-03T18:35:30", "kind": "benchmark", "agent": "tool", "summary": "test_prefilter {'gap_min': 0.7, 'gap_max': 1.2, 'any_of_elements': ['Bi', 'Sb', 'Sn', 'Ge', 'Cu']}: recall 0.163, removed 0.984 of non-hits", "evidence": {"gap_min": 0.7, "gap_max": 1.2, "any_of_elements": ["Bi", "Sb", "Sn", "Ge", "Cu"]}}, {"id": "8fd2e24e", "time": "2026-10-03T18:35:41", "kind": "result", "agent": "runner", "summary": "Round 2 Step 0 ABORT: prefilter (gap 0.7–1.2 eV + any_of [Bi,Sb,Sn,Ge,Cu]) fails both abort-gate thresholds — recall 16.3% (< 60%) and sub-pool size 41 (< 50). Step 1 compare_strategies NOT executed per plan.", "evidence": "test_prefilter raw output: {"rule": {"gap_min": 0.7, "gap_max": 1.2, "any_of_elements": ["Bi", "Sb", "Sn", "Ge", "Cu"]}, "pool_before": 1362, "pool_after": 41, "hits_before": 129, "hits_after": 21, "hit_recall": 0.163, "non_hits_removed": 0.984, "hit_rate_